hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20955","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ali, meaning Ibn Mubarak, narrated to us from Yahya, Hayyah al-Tamimi narrated to me that his father informed him that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Nothing in hamah, and the evil eye is true, and the truest of omens is the good omen."
"20956","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Hayyah ibn Habis al-Tamimi narrated to me that his father informed him that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Nothing in hamah, and the evil eye is true, and the truest of divination is the good omen."
"20957","Abd al-Samad and Hasan ibn Musa and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Shayban narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Hayyah, he narrated to him from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Nothing in hamah, and the evil eye is true, and the truest of omens is the good omen."
